# Faith Feast

Faith Feast is a community-first food delivery platform built around a single daily drop model, fair driver pay, and a mobile-first user experience.

## Product vision

- Customers receive one curated daily food drop instead of endless scrolling.
- Vendors list limited-edition kitchen drops with real-time inventory management.
- Drivers keep 100% of tips and delivery fees, with no platform fee taken from earnings.
- The app runs as a Progressive Web App so users can install Faith Feast directly on their home screen.

## Stack

- Next.js 14
- React
- Tailwind-inspired CSS with custom styling
- PostgreSQL schema for users, vendors, drops, orders, and driver payouts
- PWA manifest and install prompt support

## Included workspace

This repository now includes:

- Homepage countdown and menu preview
- Customer order flow and checkout experience
- Vendor dashboard for menu/inventory management
- Driver dashboard for transparent earnings
- Login and signup page for multiple account types
- SQL schema for the product database
- API route stubs for auth, drops, orders, and driver earnings

## Run locally

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Then open: http://localhost:3000

## Notes

This is a working product prototype and frontend flow. The API routes currently use in-memory mock data for demo purposes, while the `db/schema.sql` file defines the production-ready PostgreSQL structure.

## Future roadmap

- Connect the app to a real Postgres database
- Add email/password authentication and session management
- Build vendor inventory editing and admin controls
- Add actual payment payout flows for drivers
- Turn the mock dashboard into a full transactional multi-role app
